---
<<if $GBBranch == true>>
    <<set $Speaker to "Player">>
    <<Update_CurrentSpeaker>>
    <<update_coral_points_display>>
    You approach the coral, and it looked like it was thinking hard about something...

    You sneaked around the coral and whispered.

    <<set $Speaker to "Player">>
    <<Update_CurrentSpeaker>>
    You: Hey, what are you thinking about?

    <<set $Speaker to "GroovedBrainCoral">>
    <<Update_CurrentSpeaker>>
    Grooved Brain Coral: WOWZERS! Jeez you are as silent as a parrot fish! How long have you been creeping behind me?

    <<set $Speaker to "Player_happy">>
    <<Update_CurrentSpeaker>>
    You were about to reply to the coral when it interrupted you excitedly.
    <<set $Speaker to "GroovedBrainCoral_happy">>
    <<Update_CurrentSpeaker>>
    Grooved Brain Coral: Actually, now that you're here, let's exchange a few fun facts about ourselves to get to know each other better!
    Grooved Brain Coral: ME FIRST!!!!!
    Grooved Brain Coral: (Clears throat)
    Grooved Brain Coral: Did you know that corals are actually animals, not plants?
    Grooved Brain Coral: And, and! White sandy beaches are actually made of corals and parrot fish excrement from feeding on corals.
    Grooved Brain Coral: Ahhh.. such is the circle of life.... I love biology..
    -> Wow, how interesting. I've learned so much in such a short time! [3 Identification Needed]
        <<identifyCorals>>
        <<set $Speaker to "GroovedBrainCoral_happy">>
