title: Grooved_Brain_Coral_Node3
position: -134,568
---
<<if $GBBranch3 == true>>
    <<set $Speaker to "Player_happy">>
    <<Update_CurrentSpeaker>>
    You happily swam towards Grooved Brain Coral but it looked really troubled...

    <<set $Speaker to "Player">>
    <<Update_CurrentSpeaker>>
    You: Hey, are you alright? You look very down.

    You waited for a response but it doesn't seem like it heard you.
    You waved your pectoral fin and repeated yourself.

    <<set $Speaker to "BleachedGroovedBrainCoral">>
    <<Update_CurrentSpeaker>>
    The coral jolted, and its eyes focused on you. It seemed to have only just realised that you were standing in front of it.

    Grooved Brain Coral: Oh, hey... Sorry, I didn't see you there. I was deep in thought and...
    The coral was about to continue when you noticed something shocking...

    <<set $Speaker to "Player">>
    <<Update_CurrentSpeaker>>
    You: Y-Your body... it's turning white! What's happening to you?
    <<set $Speaker to "BleachedGroovedBrainCoral">>
    <<Update_CurrentSpeaker>>
    Grooved Brain Coral: Oh, you don't have to worry. It's just the bleaching...
    Grooved Brain Coral: The water is getting too warm, and I'm losing the tiny algae that give me my colour and help me survive.
    -> Are you talking about your zooxanthellae?
        Grooved Brain Coral: Yes, without them, I'm getting sick...
    -> Are you talking about your Symbiodiniaceae? [3 Identification Needed]
        <<identifyCorals>>
        <<set $SWCoralPoints += 5>>
        <<update_coral_points_display>>
        Grooved Brain Coral: Wow, you must have done your homework. I'm pleasantly surprised you know this term...
    
    <<set $Speaker to "Player">>
    <<Update_CurrentSpeaker>>
    You: Is there anything I can do to help?
    <<set $Speaker to "BleachedGroovedBrainCoral">>
    <<Update_CurrentSpeaker>>
    Grooved Brain Coral: Fret not! My superior intellect will save me from this predicament!
    <<set $Speaker to "Player">>
    <<Update_CurrentSpeaker>>
    You: Come on, there must be something I can do!
    <<set $Speaker to "BleachedGroovedBrainCoral">>
    <<Update_CurrentSpeaker>>
    Grooved Brain Coral: I appreciate your concern, but this is beyond your understanding. I know my own condition better than anyone... and your efforts may only make things worse.
    <<set $Speaker to "None">>
    <<Update_CurrentSpeaker>>
    Grooved Brain Coral's voice grows weaker with every word. It is slowly losing energy and may not be able to continue the conversation for much longer. There is absolutely no way it can solve this by itself.
    <<set $Speaker to "Player">>
    <<Update_CurrentSpeaker>>
    You: Can you drop the almighty act for a moment and let me help you? 
    You: You're clearly not in a state to handle this alone.
    <<set $Speaker to "BleachedGroovedBrainCoral">>
    <<Update_CurrentSpeaker>>
    Grooved Brain Coral: I-It's not that I don't want you to help... 
    Grooved Brain Coral: I just...
    Grooved Brain Coral: This is something I need to do by myself.
    Grooved Brain Coral: Do you remember... the story I told you when we first met... That day, everything changed...
    Grooved Brain Coral: I was still a budding coral, basking in the sunlight, when a parrotfish swam up to me.
    Grooved Brain Coral: It asked if I knew where to find a colony of Grooved Brain Corals.
    <<set $Speaker to "BleachedGroovedBrainCoral_sad">>
